  "findings": {
    "bao": "Fixture passed raw temporary paths to a validator that explicitly rejects noncanonical checkpoint spelling. Only owned test roots were normalized; original production guard and both tests remain. Exact historical failing path was not printed.",
    "fleet": "Rust1.96 Apple sync_all directly invokes F_FULLFSYNC, without an ordinary fsync fallback. The historical errno13 messages do not identify the failing operation; existing cfg(test) release-install stage instrumentation is needed. No permission or ordering change made.",
    "holdout": "Apple File::try_lock uses flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB). The two failures immediately follow store drop while other tests in the same library harness spawn subprocesses. Inherited open-file descriptions are a possible cause, not an observed cause. No unconditional Drop.unlock added.",
    "acceptance_difference": "Original MacARM failures used one Bazel library process with multiple parallel tests. A nextest per-test-process pass alone would not disprove a cross-test spawn-inheritance failure."
  },
